bron was built seven years before Zoan in Egypt.)¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÇAnd they came unto the brook of Eshcol, and cut down from thence a branch with one cluster of grapes, and they bare it between two upon a staff; and they brought of the pomegranates, and of the figs.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙzThe place was called the brook Eshcol, because of the cluster of grapes which the children of Israel cut down from thence.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ>And they returned from searching of the land after forty days.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙõAnd they went and came to Moses, and to Aaron, and to all the congregation of the children of Israel, unto the wilderness of Paran, to Kadesh; and brought back word unto them, and unto all the congregation, and shewed them the fruit of the land.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“And they told him, and said, We came unto the land whither thou sentest us, and surely it floweth with milk and honey; and this is the fruit of it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”Nevertheless the people be strong that dwell in the land, and the cities are walled, and very great: and moreover we saw the children of Anak there.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¾The Amalekites dwell in the land of the south: and the Hittites, and the Jebusites, and the Amorites, dwell in the mountains: and the Canaanites dwell by the sea, and by the coast of Jordan.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd Caleb stilled the people before Moses, and said, Let us go up at once, and possess it; for we are well able to overcome it.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse!¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrBut the men that went up